[[539,212,"The inquest heard evidence that patients who suffer from severe dementia who need specialist placements often spend many months in hospital whilst funding and suitable placements are being found. Given the resources available on acute hospital wards this puts these patients at risk as they cannot always be adequately supervised. I am concerned that the lengthy delays in securing funding and finding suitable placements for these most vulnerable patients creates a risk of future deaths and I consider action should be taken.","delayed funding and placement for severe dementia patients",""],[3247,1228,"Lack of inpatient mental health beds and lack of Psychiatric decisions unit (PDU) spaces","lack of inpatient mental health beds and PDU spaces",""],[3248,1228,"it is often the case that due to the lack of inpatient beds and PDU spaces patients are often left in the Emergency department unattended or sent home with periodic reviews by the home treatment team whilst waiting for a bed","lack of inpatient beds and PDU spaces",""],[3249,1228,"there is no agreed protocol to deal with informal patients who abscond from emergency departments","lack of agreed protocol for informal missing patients",""],[3250,1228,"on 2 occasions (03/12/21 and 07/12/21) there was a failure to treat Mr Hamilton as a missing person when he was reported as missing","failure to treat missing persons as high risk",""],[3251,1228,"When Mr Hamilton was first reported as missing no risk assessment was undertaken about his level of risk to himself","lack of risk assessment for missing persons",""],[3589,1351,"there is not wide knowledge of the availability of these devices in care settings and if more homes had them it is likely that deaths from choking could be reduced","lack of anti choking devices in care homes",""],[3740,1411,"There continues to be a chronic lack of resources to treat seriously mentally ill patients in Birmingham and Solihull","lack of resources",""],[3741,1411,"communication between the specialist teams is not effective enough","ineffective communication between specialist teams",""],[3742,1411,"Carbamazepine management was proposed in 2012 to manage the deceased's mental health however this was not picked up by his GP and was only noted by a BSMHFT consultant in August 2022","lack of medication management",""],[3743,1411,"different health organisations use different digital systems that do not communicate with each other","incompatible digital systems",""],[3744,1411,"current resources do not allow GPs to pro- actively check patients are collecting prescribed medication due to excessive patient lists","lack of resources",""],[8596,3291,"no bed was available in August 2022","lack of psychiatric bed capacity",""],[8597,3291,"lack of psychiatric bed capacity remains an ongoing problem","lack of psychiatric bed capacity",""],[8598,3291,"no bed was available in December 2021","lack of psychiatric bed capacity",""],[8642,3306,"significant staffing issues during the Ronald's period of in- patient care that caused delays to his treatment","staffing shortages causing treatment delays",""],[8643,3306,"patients have died, and will continue to die, from avoidable deaths due to delays caused by these staffing inadequacies","avoidable deaths from treatment delays",""],[8644,3306,"inadequate cohesive forward thinking or planning either in relation short term pressures (eg.","lack of forward planning for seasonal pressures",""]]